                <pb facs="0936" n="816" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg816"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A 4e/11: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-03-11T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 11,
                                1922—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 14—12
                    noon.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>98. Your 44, February 25, 3 p.m.<anchor n="88" xml:id="d608-f1"/> communicated to
                    the Chinese Government. Foreign Office circular note dated 10th to different
                    Legations announces that Chinese Government has appointed its delegates for
                    effective 5 percent revision and has set March 31st at Shanghai for opening of
                    conference. Note requests immediate appointment of delegates and notification of
                    names.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
